WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.680
"Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings"&nbsp;
tells a complete, self-contained origin story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.920
while also setting up future adventures&nbsp;
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.040
Not everything is neatly tied&nbsp;
up at the end of the story. Here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.720
are some of the biggest unanswered&nbsp;
questions left open by "Shang-Chi."

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.880
Perhaps the worst kept secret&nbsp;
about "Shang-Chi and the Legend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.640
of the Ten Rings" was the involvement&nbsp;
of Ben Kingsley as Trevor Slattery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.200
who first entered the Marvel Cinematic&nbsp;
Universe in 2013's "Iron Man 3."

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.880
"I wouldn't go in there for twenty minutes."

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.280
If Ben Kingsley's red carpet arrivals didn't&nbsp;
make it clear, his surprise appearance at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:42.000
the "Shang-Chi" press conference solidified&nbsp;
it. His role wasn't a mere bit part, either:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.200
Trevor proved critical to the plot, and our&nbsp;
heroes could never have found Ta-Lo without him.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.520
While the audience sees what happens&nbsp;
to Shang-Chi, Katy, and Xialing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:56.400
Trevor just kind of vanishes. He survives&nbsp;
the attack of the so-called "soul-suckers"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.800
by playing dead, which might be the greatest&nbsp;
performance of the desperate actor's career.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.520
But what about us, the audience? We never&nbsp;
learn if he stayed in the village, if he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:11.120
left with Shang-Chi and the gang, or began his&nbsp;
own acting troupe among the residents of Ta-Lo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.000
Sir Ben Kingsley is one of&nbsp;
the best parts of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.320
so here's hoping we don't have to wait another&nbsp;
seven years to find out what happened to him.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.800
"And you'll never see me coming."

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.520
One of the last things we hear before&nbsp;
the credits roll is that Xialing is at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.880
her father's base to dismantle his operations.&nbsp;
Then, the post-credits scene reveals that Xialing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.080
did indeed show up at the Ten Rings base, but&nbsp;
most certainly did not dismantle it. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.600
she takes the throne herself as men&nbsp;
and women train in the courtyard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.000
seemingly preparing themselves to take&nbsp;
down whatever targets Xialing may select.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.440
We're promised the Ten Rings will&nbsp;
return, which means that one way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:52.480
or another we'll get a definitive answer to&nbsp;
what Xialing plans on doing with her new crew.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:56.160
We don't know whether she was always&nbsp;
lying about taking apart her dad's toxic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:00.480
infrastructure, or if she just had a&nbsp;
potentially sinister change of heart.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:05.280
We also don't know how noble she'll be in her&nbsp;
new role. Although her story in "Shang-Chi"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:10.480
seemed to end in a positive place, she's still&nbsp;
now lost both of her parents. There's no telling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.560
how that may have affected her outlook.&nbsp;
Did Xialing's underground fighting outfit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.680
The Golden Daggers Club get folded into this new&nbsp;
business venture? We'll have to wait to find out.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:26.720
Shang-Chi and Katy are best friends, and have&nbsp;
such natural chemistry that Katy's own grandmother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:31.280
asks when the two are going to get married. At&nbsp;
no point in the movie is any kind of romantic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.040
relationship discussed or even really&nbsp;
implied between them -- and yet their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.200
story still follows something resembling&nbsp;
a traditional "friends-to-lovers" arc.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.520
The only thing is, they never officially&nbsp;
become lovers. By the end of the movie they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:47.920
are walking arm-in-arm with each other, and&nbsp;
certainly seem closer than when they started.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:52.640
Is that the only hint we get about their&nbsp;
relationship status? What exactly is their deal?

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.800
"Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings"&nbsp;
director Destin Daniel Cretton addressed this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.040
point during a "Shang-Chi" press conference&nbsp;
attended by Looper. When asked if Shang-Chi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.880
and Katy were meant to be best friends&nbsp;
or potential love interests, he asked,

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.360
"Aren't all friendships potential love interests?"

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.600
He went on to say that the relationship between&nbsp;
Shang-Chi and Katy was written as being intimate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:16.080
caring, but also strictly platonic. But&nbsp;
he also said there's another reason why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:21.040
Shaun and Katy don't end their adventure with&nbsp;
a big romantic smooch. As the director put it,

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.600
"It also just naturally felt like the only way&nbsp;
to go with this movie, because Shang-Chi is so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:29.760
deep in his own inner struggle. I don't think&nbsp;
there's emotional space for anything else."

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.560
What's left unanswered is what happens next -—&nbsp;
after all, Shang-Chi's arc in the movie is him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.880
finally coming to terms with his upbringing&nbsp;
and inner turmoil. Now that he's got a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.520
more emotional space, will these two stay&nbsp;
friends forever, or become something more?

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:48.800
Fittingly, "Shang-Chi and the Legend of&nbsp;
the Ten Rings" begins with a legend. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.320
start with the story of Wenwu using&nbsp;
his powers to conquer his enemies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.440
while the narration speculates&nbsp;
about the origin of the rings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:00.080
Possibilities like the rings being found in a&nbsp;
cave are mentioned, but nothing is ever declared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:05.840
the truth — and that's the sum total of what we&nbsp;
know about the MCU-official origins of his power.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:10.240
In the comics, the rings arrived on&nbsp;
Earth many years ago with Fin Fang Foom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:14.320
the extraterrestrial, shape-shifting&nbsp;
lizard-dragon-alien thing who may or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.960
may not be present in "Shang-Chi" in the&nbsp;
form of the giant monster that kills Wenwu.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:24.160
The Mandarin tore his spaceship apart looking for&nbsp;
artifacts, and that's how he got his ten rings.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.640
But none of this is mentioned in the movie,&nbsp;
and we are told that Wenwu, aka The Mandarin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:34.480
has possessed these rings for ten lifetimes. So,&nbsp;
were they the result of some kind of 11th-century&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:38.960
treasure hunt? Was Wenwu seeking them out? We&nbsp;
know at the end that the rings have some kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:44.000
beacon — were they reaching out to him? Or were&nbsp;
they reaching out to somewhere in outer space,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.600
calling for some alien force to&nbsp;
come to Earth and come after them?

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:52.000
It's almost certain that we'll learn more about&nbsp;
the lineage of the Ten Rings at some point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:56.240
But as for how Wenwu found them in the&nbsp;
first place? That remains to be seen.

